<title>MEXICO: Bital chief to lead Mexico banking group.</title>
<headline>Bital chief to lead Mexico banking group.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Grupo Financiero Bital president Antonio del Valle Ruiz was chosen by the directors of the Mexican Bankers Association to lead the group, an association spokesman said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The group's previous president was Jose Madariaga, who held the post for more than two years. Madariaga, president of Grupo Financiero BBV-Probursa, is leaving the post because his term has run out.</p>
<p>Del Valle's term officially begins in March at the association's annual convention in March, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>((--Cecilia Cardenas, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9552))</p>
